<!--
    Objective-C methods that pass or return an aggregate by value.

    Issue: a method whose type encoding spells a union (`(Word=qf)`) or a
    struct with no name (`{?=ii}`) by value decoded that argument to void, so
    the method lost its whole prototype: `long -[Shape word:](void *a0,
    unsigned long a1, long a2)` reading `((long *)a0)[0x12]`, with no `self`.
    A struct with bit-fields (`{Flags=b3b5S}`) was laid out with one 4-byte
    word per bit-field, 12 bytes for a 4-byte struct, so the model placed it in
    two registers.

    Fix: `encoding.rs (struct_type)` builds the struct or union the encoding
    spells with the C layout of its members (natural alignment, a run of
    bit-fields as the bytes it packs into, union members at offset zero), names
    an unnamed one from its member codes, and the calling convention's own
    rules place it: a homogeneous floating-point aggregate in d0..d3, up to 16
    bytes in x registers, anything larger by pointer, and a return past 16
    bytes through x8.

    One pass, the fixed output.
-->
